# Phase-4 replay archive — the creation-before-operation invariant on the
# judging side: a pickup that beats its own spawn report names an item whose
# creation this host has never judged. It is refused AT ONCE — no hold window,
# no guess, no waiting for the creation to maybe arrive — and the late spawn
# report still registers idempotently afterwards, so the item simply stays in
# the world and nobody owns it.
#
# The SENDER's half of the invariant (settle every deferred creation report
# before reporting an operation on the same item) is what keeps this shape
# unreachable in a correct session; this file pins the host's answer when a peer
# breaks the rule. The old 500 ms hold lived here and is gone rather than kept
# as a fallback.
#
# Mechanism: KernelProtocolCommandHandler.TryRefuseUnjudgedOperation

@0 pickup g1 42 test_item 1.0
@0 fault g1 host delay=300
@0 spawn g1 42 test_item 1.0
@33 expect reject g1 42
@33 expect no_host_table 42
@333 expect host_table 42 within 500
